{
  "id": "COMPOUND:2734 - PROTEIN:6293",
  "verbalization": "Stanolone is implicated in the regulation of Dipeptidyl peptidase IX (DPPX) through multiple indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Stanolone acts as a target for several enzymes, including 11-cis retinol dehydrogenase and 5-Alpha-Androstane-3-Beta,17beta-Diol, which in turn target DPPX. These enzymes are involved in metabolic pathways that are often linked to the regulation of gene expression and cellular function. The presence of multiple targets for Stanolone, each of which has a direct interaction with DPPX, indicates a potential mechanism by which Stanolone influences DPPX activity. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Stanolone and DPPX, emphasizing the role of metabolic enzymes in modulating the activity of DPPX. The evidence supports a network of interactions where Stanolone indirectly affects DPPX through its targets, suggesting a broader regulatory role in cellular processes.",
